WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.982
- [Voiceover] Let's say
that we have the equation

00:01.982 --> 00:06.841
six plus three w is equal to

00:06.841 --> 00:11.822
the square root of two w plus 12

00:11.822 --> 00:14.207
plus two w.

00:14.207 --> 00:17.648
See if you can pause the
video and solve for w,

00:17.648 --> 00:19.248
and it might have more than one solution,

00:19.248 --> 00:20.877
so keep that in mind.

00:20.877 --> 00:22.779
Alright, now let's work
through this together.

00:22.779 --> 00:23.836
So the first thing I'd like to do

00:23.836 --> 00:25.274
whenever I see one of
these radical equations

00:25.274 --> 00:28.112
is just isolate the radical
on one side of the equation.

00:28.112 --> 00:31.492
So let's subtract two w from both sides.

00:31.492 --> 00:33.696
I want to get rid of that two
w from the right-hand side.

00:33.696 --> 00:35.266
I just want the radical sign.

00:35.266 --> 00:38.133
And if I subtract two w from both sides,

00:38.133 --> 00:39.552
what am I left with?

00:39.552 --> 00:42.276
Well, on the left-hand
side, I am left with

00:42.276 --> 00:45.343
six plus three w minus two w.

00:45.343 --> 00:47.300
Well, three of something
take away two of 'em,

00:47.300 --> 00:48.910
you're going to be left with w.

00:48.910 --> 00:51.144
Six plus w is equal to,

00:51.144 --> 00:52.955
these cancel out, we're left with

00:52.955 --> 00:57.242
the square root of two w plus 12.

00:57.242 --> 00:58.660
And to get rid of the radical,

00:58.660 --> 01:00.743
we're going to square both sides,

01:00.743 --> 01:03.158
and we've seen before that
this process right over here,

01:03.158 --> 01:04.063
it's a little bit tricky,

01:04.063 --> 01:04.949
because when you're squaring a radical

01:04.949 --> 01:06.911
in a radical equation like this,

01:06.911 --> 01:11.016
and then you solve, you might
find an extraneous solution.

01:11.016 --> 01:12.133
What do I mean by that?

01:12.133 --> 01:13.370
Well, we're going to get the same result

01:13.370 --> 01:16.068
whether we square this or
whether we square that,

01:16.068 --> 01:18.454
because when you square a
negative, it becomes a positive.

01:18.454 --> 01:21.080
But those are fundamentally
two different equations.

01:21.080 --> 01:22.800
We only want the solutions that satisfy

01:22.800 --> 01:24.672
the one that doesn't
have the negative there.

01:24.672 --> 01:26.181
So that's why we're going
to test our solutions

01:26.181 --> 01:29.260
to make sure they're valid
for our original equation.

01:29.260 --> 01:31.041
So, if we square both sides,

01:31.041 --> 01:34.995
on the left-hand side,
we're going to have,

01:34.995 --> 01:37.319
well, it's gonna be w squared

01:37.319 --> 01:40.459
plus two times their product.

01:40.459 --> 01:43.603
So, two times six times w, so that's 12 w,

01:43.603 --> 01:46.476
plus six squared, 36,

01:46.476 --> 01:50.159
Is equal to, now, if
you take the square root

01:50.159 --> 01:53.962
and square it, you're going to
be left with two plus twelve.

01:53.962 --> 01:58.429
Now, we can subtract two
w and 12 from both sides,

01:58.429 --> 01:59.648
so let's do that.

01:59.648 --> 02:02.385
So then we can get it into
a standard quadratic form.

02:02.385 --> 02:05.827
So let's subtract two w from both sides

02:05.827 --> 02:09.479
and let's subtract 12 from both sides.

02:09.479 --> 02:11.562
So, subtract 12 from the right.

02:11.562 --> 02:12.558
Subtract 12 here.

02:12.558 --> 02:13.795
And once again, I just
want to get rid of this

02:13.795 --> 02:15.104
on the right-hand side,

02:15.104 --> 02:17.670
and I'm going to be left with,

02:17.670 --> 02:20.266
I am going to be left with,

02:20.266 --> 02:22.259
on the left-hand side, it's gonna be

02:22.259 --> 02:23.677
w squared.

02:23.677 --> 02:27.300
See, 12 w minus two w is plus ten w,

02:27.300 --> 02:30.700
and then 36 minus twelve is plus 24,

02:30.700 --> 02:34.112
is equal to zero.

02:34.112 --> 02:35.440
Now, let's see, to solve this,

02:35.440 --> 02:36.427
let's see, is this factorable?

02:36.427 --> 02:38.892
Are there two numbers that up to ten

02:38.892 --> 02:40.734
and whose product is 24?

02:40.734 --> 02:43.299
What jumps out at me is six and four.

02:43.299 --> 02:46.318
So we can rewrite this as w plus four

02:46.318 --> 02:50.393
times w plus six is equal to zero.

02:50.393 --> 02:52.476
And so, if I have the
product of two things

02:52.476 --> 02:53.713
equaling zero,

02:53.713 --> 02:55.856
well to solve this,
either one or both of them

02:55.856 --> 02:56.732
could be equal zero.

02:56.732 --> 02:58.301
Zero times anything is gonna be zero.

02:58.301 --> 03:01.848
So, w plus four is equal to zero,

03:01.848 --> 03:05.572
or w plus six is equal to zero.

03:05.572 --> 03:07.835
And over here, if you
subtract four from both sides,

03:07.835 --> 03:10.401
you get w is equal to negative four.

03:10.401 --> 03:12.811
Or, subtract six from both sides here.

03:12.811 --> 03:14.678
w is equal to negative six.

03:14.678 --> 03:17.847
Now let's verify that these
actually are solutions

03:17.847 --> 03:18.873
to our original equation.

03:18.873 --> 03:20.141
Remember, our original equation was six.

03:20.141 --> 03:22.073
I'll rewrite it here.

03:22.073 --> 03:25.001
Our original equation was six plus three w

03:25.001 --> 03:29.981
is equal to the square
root of two w plus 12

03:29.981 --> 03:32.125
plus two w.

03:32.125 --> 03:35.022
So let's see, if w is
equal to negative four,

03:35.022 --> 03:38.571
if w is equal to negative four right over,

03:38.571 --> 03:40.050
let me do something different,

03:40.050 --> 03:41.680
is equal to negative four.

03:41.680 --> 03:45.574
So, that's going to be six
plus three times negative four

03:45.574 --> 03:50.574
is equal to the square root
of two times negative four

03:50.705 --> 03:54.599
plus 12 plus two times negative four.

03:54.599 --> 03:58.644
So this would be, this
is, negative twelve here.

03:58.644 --> 04:00.867
This is negative eight here.

04:00.867 --> 04:02.937
This is negative eight here,

04:02.937 --> 04:06.789
so you have six plus negative
twelve, which is negative six,

04:06.789 --> 04:11.769
is equal to the square root
of negative eight plus 12,

04:11.769 --> 04:15.814
is four, plus negative eight.

04:15.814 --> 04:17.565
So that would be negative six is equal to

04:17.565 --> 04:19.647
two plus negative eight,

04:19.647 --> 04:21.187
which is absolutely true.

04:21.187 --> 04:23.602
So this is definitely a solution.

04:23.602 --> 04:26.952
And let's try w is equal to negative six.

04:26.952 --> 04:30.303
So, we is equal to negative six.

04:30.303 --> 04:33.100
So, we're gonna get, if we look
up here, we're going to have

04:33.100 --> 04:36.469
six plus three times negative six

04:36.469 --> 04:40.819
is equal to the square root
of two times negative six

04:40.819 --> 04:45.083
plus 12 plus two w.

04:45.083 --> 04:47.888
So, this is gonna be negative 18.

04:47.888 --> 04:49.929
This is going to be negative 12.

04:49.929 --> 04:50.663
This is negative 12.

04:50.663 --> 04:51.925
Negative 12 plus 12 is zero.

04:51.925 --> 04:54.483
Square root of zero, this is always zero.

04:54.483 --> 04:55.896
And then two times,

04:55.896 --> 04:58.432
and actually let me, I shouldn't
have written a w there,

04:58.432 --> 05:00.364
I should have written
two times negative six.

05:00.364 --> 05:01.662
So back to what I was doing,

05:01.662 --> 05:04.559
this right over here is negative eighteen.

05:04.559 --> 05:08.000
This is two times negative six plus 12.

05:08.000 --> 05:10.351
This is all zero.

05:10.351 --> 05:11.474
Square root of zero is zero.

05:11.474 --> 05:14.552
And then this is negative twelve.

05:14.552 --> 05:16.193
So you get six plus negative of eighteen

05:16.193 --> 05:17.844
which is negative 12.

05:17.844 --> 05:19.806
Is equal to zero plus negative 12.

05:19.806 --> 05:20.923
Negative 12.

05:20.923 --> 05:22.643
Which is absolutely correct.

05:22.643 --> 05:24.485
So these are actually both solutions

05:24.485 --> 05:27.453
to our original radical equation.
